From: pugant <pugant@localhost>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 18:17:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/19] tests: mini qwen4exp generator + decode-graph node dump
 + bit-exact hashes [w6-2]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

P3 attribution instrument for the A1-C1 card: writes a synthetic tiny
qwen4exp GGUF (trunk+MTP and draft-only variants) exercising every decode
path (GDN recurrent layers, full-attention QSA with the selection active,
PLE layer, hyper-connection mixers, MoE with separate gate/up experts), then
runs a fixed decode schedule (prefill 8 + N single-token steps + one
3-token batch + 3 MTP drafter steps with h input) on CPU with n_rs_seq=16.

--dump installs the eval callback and prints one line per computed node
(op, name, shape, contiguity, bytes, FNV-1a hash of the data, src ops,
nearest named ancestor) — the per-call-site attribution of the graph's
CPY/CONT population. The logits hash per eval and the full context-state
hash are the bit-exact probe used to compare a baseline build against a
copy-elimination build (all weights/inputs from a seeded LCG).

Built but not registered in ctest: a standalone run only asserts that the
schedule completes, while the gate is a diff between two builds' outputs.

Artifacts of the attribution run: logs/wave6/w6m2-attribuzione.txt,
w6m2-dump-{BASE,PATCH}.txt, w6m2-mini{,-draft}.gguf.

Co-Authored-By: GLM by z.ai <glm@z.ai>
